From 68225c3d5da5a530705bd77d2110fb3bbbbb6a80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 01:40:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0151: re-apply the HUD shift after the game's forced
 recompute; fix hide->show deadlock; match the MapMiniPlayer needle

S1: the per-frame layout driver (0xa1cb80) restores a counter All pane's
local to base and recomposes +0x70 from it AFTER the +0x13c hook and
BEFORE Draw, via the forced recompute 0x9036cc -> 0x909d4c (only caller
the driver at 0xa1cdf8, force=1), bypassing both Calculate cuts -- the
#66 wipe (only the compass moved). New third cut at 0x909da0, inside
0x909d4c after its own recompute and before its children loop, so the
same hud_edge re-applies the shift there. Neither in-Calculate recompute
path can do this: both run before the +0x13c cut and recompose from the
hook's own shifted values.
S2: move the bit-7 guard to after the matcher -- a hidden pane's
Calculate early-exits (0x90969c/0x9096a4) and clears bit 7, so the old
guard skipped it forever and hide->show was dead. A matched pane with
a table entry is never skipped now; a never-calculated pane with no
entry is still skipped on its first frame.
S3: an All with a PicView direct child matches compass (MapMiniPlayer's
red needle; MapPlayer's PicView sits under Icon00, so the full-screen
map does not match).
Also: hud_probe.c / hud_manual.c stale table-layout comments (96x128,
16 slots -> 66x176, 11 slots); hud_edge_mark_dirty comment corrected
(bit 4 -> CalculateLocalMatrix 0x9096d0 from the pane's own components,
not the bit-5 global computation).
---
 dm/games/0100000000010000/hud_probe.c   |   8 +-
 dm/games/0100000000010000/hud_runtime.c |  92 ++++++++++--
 dm/games/0100000000010000/patches.py    | 185 +++++++++++++++---------
 dm/host/hud_manual.c                    |   2 +-
 4 files changed, 204 insertions(+), 83 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/games/0100000000010000/hud_probe.c b/dm/games/0100000000010000/hud_probe.c
index 37098f2..60d95fc 100644
--- a/dm/games/0100000000010000/hud_probe.c
+++ b/dm/games/0100000000010000/hud_probe.c
@@ -198,9 +198,11 @@ typedef unsigned long uintptr_t;
 #define HP_R_W2 88
 #define HP_R_W3 92
 
-// The hud_edge table (must match hud_edge.c): 96 entries of 128 bytes,
-// sixteen slots per element; entry +0 the pane, +104/+108/+112 the applied
-// dx/dy/k, +116 the hidden flag, +120 the element index, +124 the valid flag.
+// The hud_edge table (must match hud_runtime.c): 66 entries of 176 bytes,
+// eleven slots per element; entry +0 the pane, +104/+108/+112 the applied
+// dx/dy/k, +116 the hidden flag, +120 the element index, +124 the valid flag,
+// +128 the original local matrix (e_lm0, 12 floats). (0151: was 96 x 128,
+// 16 slots -- stale since 0150.)
 #define HUD_EDGE_N 6
 #define HUD_EDGE_ENTRY 128
 #define HUD_EDGE_SLOTS_PER_ELEM 16
